preConditionHook:
// RISK ONE UNIT TO MAKE R UNITS -- Brooks's trade management, parameterized
// stop-first: stopDollars IS the risk and rewardRisk is the R multiple, so the
// two axes a grid wants to sweep are the two inputs.
// Behaviourally this is TakeProfitWithRatioStop re-parameterized
// (target = rewardRisk * stopDollars, stopRatio = 1 / rewardRisk); it is
// authored anyway because that rule's axes are the TARGET and a stop fraction,
// which sweeps a different lattice of (stop, target) pairs for the same grid
// budget. It replaces StopAtInitialRiskMultiple and
// ProfitTargetAtInitialRiskMultiple (B09, Not written), which were blocked on an
// initial-risk accessor the engine does not have: a fixed dollar risk is the
// cheap, honest stand-in for the entry-frozen risk those rules wanted.
// Direction-agnostic, so both sides are identical text, as in StopLoss and
// TakeProfit. The profit accessor, the sign convention and the tolerance-
// carrying comparisons are TakeProfitWithRatioStop's verbatim; OpenPositionProfit
// is close-marked and net of the ENTRY side's costs (VERIFIED). No
// MarketPosition guard: both generators already gate an exit on the position at
// signal time, exactly as StopLoss and TakeProfitWithRatioStop rely on.
